            "created_at": "2025-08-27T23:23:34.547358+00:00",
            "notes": "[Pulse Converter](item_a93a8a8e-28d1-4b02-8d80-3234f9eea3dc) is the best bang for your buck, and it'll make sure you never waste the half-second of auto-aim you get from [Super Visor](item_b3db0ab0-26b4-4d99-893d-175f6726c9e9) by having to reload during it.\n\n[Shieldbuster](item_9ee1f150-537d-40b9-b975-7820fb1c6a66) is great for burning away the armor/shields of enemy tanks, and can be even better if some of the squishier opponents picked up armor or shields for defense. It's great if you can coordinate with your team to burst down tanks, but even if not, it'll help you put out as much damage as possible to pressure the enemy team and make more money.\n\nIf you're up against an enemy Junker Queen, don't take [Shieldbuster](item_9ee1f150-537d-40b9-b975-7820fb1c6a66), as you won't be able to proc its effect reliably and you won't get as much out of it.\n\nIf you've got more cash than the build accounts for at this point, buy some of the optional blues. [Custom Stock](item_17d633af-8bcc-4893-b865-be0a7bc66fe2) is often a great pick since it's very cheap and boosts both your weapon damage and rockets.\n\nAs your item slots start filling up, sell greens for space rather than splurging on purple items too early. You'll usually get more value out of 3 blues and 3 greens than 1 purple and 5 greens.\n\n[Phantasmic Flux](item_5e644a79-cf6e-4196-8d0a-232f75004643) is the best pick if you have any issues with survivability whatsoever at this point.\n\nIf the enemy team isn't putting any pressure on you at all, getting [Superflexor](item_580b77b4-0d63-469b-99a8-5372c55dfc1b) first is probably the optimal pick, but Soldier is often a target for burst damage that will take you down quickly like missile dives from Diva or aimed shots from Freya. [Phantasmic Flux](item_5e644a79-cf6e-4196-8d0a-232f75004643) is often enough to help you survive those targeted attacks at this point and stay in the fight longer, while also giving you some extra damage output.\n\nIf sticking with your team means you're getting hit by a lot of incidental effects (burns from Ashe's dynamite, chained sleeps from Ana, Junker Queen's Rampage ult, etc.), consider picking up a [Cushioned Padding](item_20f2f4bc-4611-4d1f-b653-20f04d56b96f). It's reasonably cheap, and 40% reduced negative effect duration is huge \u2013 for burns, it's 40% less damage, and it makes it much easier to keep yourself alive and topped up with biotic field. It also means if there's an enemy Ashe burning you, she'll be doing less damage, getting less money, and is less likely to snowball into a powerhouse.\n\nIf you're up against enemy flyers, [Stratosphere Beacon](item_15bf2dc7-5161-47b0-929b-17cbb1d54182) is probably a stronger pick than [Shieldbuster](item_9ee1f150-537d-40b9-b975-7820fb1c6a66). Your goal is still to put out as much damage as possible on any target, but [Super Visor](item_b3db0ab0-26b4-4d99-893d-175f6726c9e9) will come in handy for proccing [Stratosphere Beacon](item_15bf2dc7-5161-47b0-929b-17cbb1d54182)'s effect.",
